Negative control for the scene rail's real component (D9 · S5 · AC2.5).

Replaces the ui `Stepper` with a hand-rolled `<ol>` of numbered buttons — the
same numbers, the same texts, the same scrub write, and the same test key — so
what is lost is only the thing the ruling names: the rail IS a `packages/ui`
component, never markup imitating one. The playhead mapping, the styles and the
model are untouched, so a spec that merely counts pills or clicks one still
passes; what goes red is the claim that the rail is `Stepper.ce.vue` (and with
it the stepper's own step state — `data-state`, `aria-current` — which no
hand-rolled list carries).

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: transport.spec.ts — the scene-rail cases that assert the ui Stepper is the
rail (its component/`role="group"` step semantics and the marked active scene).

Re-armed 2026-08-13 against the keep-the-stop-in-view watcher (`R6-24`): the
list keeps the template ref so the mutant changes the rail's COMPONENT and
nothing else.

